WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.733 --> 00:00:06.786
This page shows the shape of the whole term at once, so no week ever surprises you.

2
00:00:06.786 --> 00:00:17.792
Read the rhythm. Most weeks meet live. Weeks 4 and 11 are independent asynchronous learning, and in Weeks 13 and 14 the usual class window becomes office hours with no lecture.

3
00:00:17.792 --> 00:00:28.806
Note the weeks that change mode. Independent weeks have a purpose: Week 4 applies the early foundations and Week 11 is a synthesis point before the final live class. The week page always names its own mode at the top.

4
00:00:28.806 --> 00:00:39.815
Follow the five-step route. Preview before class, meet or work independently, return to finish the week, connect your class takeaways to your notes, and carry it forward into your map.

5
00:00:39.815 --> 00:00:49.961
Plan your heavy weeks early. Use the rhythm to spot where readings and due dates stack up against your other courses, then start those weeks earlier.

6
00:00:49.961 --> 00:00:52.565
Nothing here is graded.

7
00:00:52.565 --> 00:00:58.366
Where next: Open Calendar and Due Dates to put exact dates against this rhythm.
